{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193048-red-talons-in-packs-with-homid-garou","id":1193048,"title":"Red Talons in packs with homid Garou?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-08T04:26:29-08:00","id":1193048,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Red Talons in packs with homid Garou?","content":"Hey,<br /> <br /> I've been recently thinking of creating a Red Talon character. So far all the knowledge I have of them is from their revised tribe book and from the core rule book of WtA 20th edition.<br /> <br /> I know for a fact that they would and do run in packs with homids, but how often does it happen? Is it that common in modern times that it'd be given if my character were to be in a pack with homid Garou?<br /> <br /> Also, while I'm already posting a question, I'll use the moment to ask for sources to learn more about the Talons. Anything will do, since I want to be able to role play it the best I can.<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance,<br /> TataCavalier<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23978-tatacavalier","name":"TataCavalier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T04:43:48-08:00","id":1193051,"title":"","content":"Well I'd say it's quiet rare since the homid would have to live as a wolf for the most part. <br /> Or it would be a more shortlived pack that is formed in a multi tribe Sept for a specific goal.<br /> <br /> On role playing, not specific to red talons, but w20 changing ways offers insight into what it feels like to be a lupus garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23979-traldar","name":"Traldar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T05:04:56-08:00","id":1193057,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the quick reply.<br /> <br /> I guess I can accept that, but while reading the tribe book I've seem references to several different packs containing homid Garou, which makes it feel like it is more common than I first thought.<br /> And yes, I would expect it to happen only within a multi-tribal sept, and not in a sept solely with Red Talons in it.<br /> <br /> And thank you! I'll make sure to read that book.<br /> <br /> I'd love more opinions about Red Talons in packs with homids, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23978-tatacavalier","name":"TataCavalier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T05:20:42-08:00","id":1193059,"title":"","content":"I think the question you have to ask yourself then is not so much why would Talons run with a homid in their pack, and more why would the homid want to be a permanent part of the Talon pack. <br /> To do so afterall would mean abandoning his human side for the most part and live as a wolf, mostly.<br /> <br /> I think the book mentions homids so much is because writes, storytellers and player's alike find homids much more relatable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23979-traldar","name":"Traldar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T05:24:46-08:00","id":1193061,"title":"","content":"Ah, I think you misunderstood my question.<br /> I do not mean that a homid would join a Red Talon dominated pack. But a multi-tribal pack which consists of 1 Red Talon and other tribes, and one or more of the packmates may be homid.<br /> <br /> It could be because they're relatable, but I believe it is to emphasize that the Red Talons can run in packs with homids and it is rather common. The reason I say that is that I remember at least 4 references to 4 different packs with homid and Talon Garou.<br /> <br /> Anywho, I'm rather new to the entire WoD scene, so I am highly unsure of what I am saying - hence, the post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23978-tatacavalier","name":"TataCavalier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T05:38:18-08:00","id":1193066,"title":"","content":"The Tribe Novels had a Red Talon in a Pack of mostly homid. And, my guess is, it can work depending on the type of stories you play and how fundamentally one wants to change the ways others behave.<br /> <br /> In the tribe novels the pack was mostly in rural areas, walking in lupus form wasn't difficult, and when they were in London, iirc they were mostly surrounded by garou and kin, so not a problem for the Red Talon to behave &quot;normally&quot; either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T05:45:56-08:00","id":1193067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TataCavalier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193048-red-talons-in-packs-with-homid-garou?p=1193061#post1193061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be because they're relatable, but I believe it is to emphasize that the Red Talons can run in packs with homids and it is rather common. The reason I say that is that I remember at least 4 references to 4 different packs with homid and Talon Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I think this is a misconception based on misleadin context.<br /> <br /> I would argue, that most Red Talons, which are in itself few, live in Red Talon septs (either as only or at least dominating tribe), and that means lupus breed only (with possibly metis).<br /> <br /> If a Red Talon was living for some reason apart from a Red Talon sept, the garou in question would onviously enter a mixed pack and therefore also join with homid. That is because a pack of multiple lupus or even multiple Red Talon woun't stay in a non-Red Talon sept. So only a sole Red Talon adopted into a sept of another tribe or multi-tribal makes sense....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T05:46:52-08:00","id":1193068,"title":"","content":"Ah ok.<br /> <br /> But I think then we are back to packs that are formed to achieve a specific goal, not so much a more permanent pack.<br /> <br /> To be Red Talons afterall is not just about the utter alienes that is your human side for any lupus born, it is about the active rejection of your human side.<br /> So I don't think a Talon could ever fell like a true part of a homid pack.<br /> There could of course be rare exceptions. But I think such a Talon would be close to leaving the Tribe, if not actually, at least philosophicly. <br /> <br /> At least that's my take on it^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23979-traldar","name":"Traldar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T06:06:23-08:00","id":1193076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193048-red-talons-in-packs-with-homid-garou?p=1193067#post1193067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I think this is a misconception based on misleadin context.<br /> <br /> I would argue, that most Red Talons, which are in itself few, live in Red Talon septs (either as only or at least dominating tribe), and that means lupus breed only (with possibly metis).<br /> <br /> If a Red Talon was living for some reason apart from a Red Talon sept, the garou in question would onviously enter a mixed pack and therefore also join with homid. That is because a pack of multiple lupus or even multiple Red Talon woun't stay in a non-Red Talon sept. So only a sole Red Talon adopted into a sept of another tribe or multi-tribal makes sense....</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you are correct, but I did read somewhere in the book that one may find at least one or two Red Talon members in mixed septs around a certain area, which I completely forgot and at the moment don't have access to the book.<br /> <br /> But yes, I am of course talking of a multi-tribal sept, not a sept dominated or solely Red Talon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traldar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193048-red-talons-in-packs-with-homid-garou?p=1193067#post1193067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I don't think a Talon could ever fell like a true part of a homid pack.<br /> There could of course be rare exceptions. But I think such a Talon would be close to leaving the Tribe, if not actually, at least philosophicly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the book says that Red Talons treat the homids in whatever packs they are in as they would any other packmate. Having the bond of the pack at the highest of levels.<br /> <br /> But, again, I think you're misunderstanding. I do not mean a pack consisting only of homids and only one lupus Red Talon.<br /> The reason I feel you may misunderstand is because you said: &quot;homid pack.&quot;<br /> <br /> But yes, I agree that it is about the active rejection of your human side, and living as a wolf. But, it is said in the tribe book that Red Talons running in packs with homids learned the English language, wore human clothes and even rode in vehicles, as to not endanger their pack and to follow their alpha.<br /> <br /> That's why I'm conflicted with answers on my question. Keep in mind I am planning on role playing the more common Red Talon, not the extremists amongst Red Talons. (Not extreme in both ways)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23978-tatacavalier","name":"TataCavalier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T06:07:17-08:00","id":1193077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193048-red-talons-in-packs-with-homid-garou?p=1193067#post1193067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Red Talon was living for some reason apart from a Red Talon sept, the garou in question would onviously enter a mixed pack and therefore also join with homid. That is because a pack of multiple lupus or even multiple Red Talon woun't stay in a non-Red Talon sept. So only a sole Red Talon adopted into a sept of another tribe or multi-tribal makes sense....</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I think lupus dominate or lupus only packs outside the Red Talons are entirely possible. Just rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23979-traldar","name":"Traldar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T06:32:18-08:00","id":1193085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TataCavalier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193048-red-talons-in-packs-with-homid-garou?p=1193076#post1193076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the book says that Red Talons treat the homids in whatever packs they are in as they would any other packmate. Having the bond of the pack at the highest of levels.<br /> <br /> But, again, I think you're misunderstanding. I do not mean a pack consisting only of homids and only one lupus Red Talon.<br /> The reason I feel you may misunderstand is because you said: &amp;quot;homid pack.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> But yes, I agree that it is about the active rejection of your human side, and living as a wolf. But, it is said in the tribe book that Red Talons running in packs with homids learned the English language, wore human clothes and even rode in vehicles, as to not endanger their pack and to follow their alpha.<br /> <br /> That's why I'm conflicted with answers on my question. Keep in mind I am planning on role playing the more common Red Talon, not the extremists amongst Red Talons. (Not extreme in both ways)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I understood. It's just that as I said, other lupus find their human side alien, but they don't actively reject it. They are open to it. <br /> What I mean is that in a mixed pack a Red Talon will never feel truly at home since he tries to utterly reject everything human in himself. Because of that he will always be somewhat disconnected from Garou who are more balanced or more human. <br /> Now, on the other hand, the simple act of trying to emphasise with his homid packmates is in itself a rather human act. Thus by doing so he would philosophicly reject part of the Red Talons philosophy. <br /> So a true Talon will never be able to reply relate to a homid packmate. This must not mean that he treats the homid different. Just that there would always be a certain distance between the to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23979-traldar","name":"Traldar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T10:17:52-08:00","id":1193190,"title":"","content":"Red Talons are great. Your concept is certainly workable, and it sounds like you are putting a fair amount of forethought into this (which is fantastic). I would give your lupus a strong reason to connect with his or her packmates. Why did your Talon leave his home sept and join with the pack in question? If you were always at this sept, is there a large community of Griffon's own there? Or are the local Talons a dying breed and you are one of their last few scions?<br /> <br /> You have figured out what breed and tribe you want to play, but you might want to get a handle on your werewolf as a character- possibly even before defining your auspice. It is easy (and common) to have a character be totally defined by their moonsign, but it isn't devastatingly interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 03-08-2018, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T10:39:12-08:00","id":1193196,"title":"","content":"Hey,<br /> <br /> -----------&gt;I've been recently thinking of creating a Red Talon character. So far all the knowledge I have of them is from their revised tribe book and from the core rule book of WtA 20th edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Well I'm glad to hear it player. Remember its not the things you know. It's the things you don't know that matter.&quot;<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> -Jerod the Glasswalker explained to the more open minded Red Talon as he tossed him some homid clothes to put on that they had to blend in with the crowd to slip past his gouls who were positioned throughout mall security to suprise the vampires who cleverly slept in a closed section of the mall. Once there they would tear those slumbering leeches to pieces.<br /> <br /> -Jerod Akbar turned to in horror to watch as the normal people stood, gawked, pointed, and a mother screamed covering her childs eyes in shock to see the Talon pack mate wearing no pans.-<br /> (Jerod)&quot; Mud-Blood!!! Where are your pans?! :O<br /> -Mud-Blood raised his his arm to reveal his left arm through the pans leg. Feeling a sense of achievement the Red Talon wagged his butt panting with tongue extended- C:<br /> (Jerod) OMFG..... -.-<br /> -Jerod- Another day at the office...<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------&gt;I know for a fact that they would and do run in packs with homids, but how often does it happen? Is it that common in modern times that it'd be given if my character were to be in a pack with homid Garou?<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes. But know most Red-Talon are closed minded and NOT subtle. During play try to always picture things from the standpoint of a wolf. The smells and what they would associate with it.. food or the scent of a rival mutt etc. Who's leader stands really, really high. And if your leader does not show alpha qualities your wolf nature will correct him in this fact.. brutally by<br /> a challenge because this is also linked to your rite to mate and this is a strong urge for them in survival. As a lupus you will do things softer homids may consider.. erm.. gross.. pissing in public on boundries is just one thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------&gt; Also, while I'm already posting a question, I'll use the moment to ask for sources to learn more about the Talons. Anything will do, since I want to be able to role play it the best I can.<br /> <br /> &quot;Try Caerns Places of Power - Red Talons Alaska (pg 77), Rage Across the world Vol. 2 (See Australian Red Talons section), of course the Red Talons Tribe book old to newer versions.<br /> If you want to get really outlandishly brutal with it also see Rage Across the Heavens (pg. 43-46 Rorg), and for an understanding of associated spirits Axis Mundi book of spirits and the Book of the Wyld in the event you play an accomplished Theurge.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Ultimately you design what you want to play and its story line which has formed its behavior up to the point of the chronicle. Remember.. you and weaver DO NOT MIX to many ends. The mating stock of the homids has killed off most of yours without being punished and in fact has been protected by other tribes instead. Inside a Red-Talon there is deeply seated anger towards that end. You are pro Wyld.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline","name":"Silentline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T08:28:11-07:00","id":1194255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193048-red-talons-in-packs-with-homid-garou?p=1193190#post1193190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Red Talons are great. Your concept is certainly workable, and it sounds like you are putting a fair amount of forethought into this (which is fantastic). I would give your lupus a strong reason to connect with his or her packmates. Why did your Talon leave his home sept and join with the pack in question? If you were always at this sept, is there a large community of Griffon's own there? Or are the local Talons a dying breed and you are one of their last few scions?<br /> <br /> You have figured out what breed and tribe you want to play, but you might want to get a handle on your werewolf as a character- possibly even before defining your auspice. It is easy (and common) to have a character be totally defined by their moonsign, but it isn't devastatingly interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the positive response. I do enjoy thinking through whatever I do before actually doing it especially when it comes to role-play characters. A strong reason to connect with his packmates would be a good idea, I honestly haven't put much thought into that but I will now, thank you!<br /> <br /> I'm also not the -most- familiar with the Red Talons, as this is going to be my first ever Red Talon character, and so I am not sure why he would've left his home sept. My first thoughts were that he had been told to join a pack with other tribes for the fight against the Wyrm, as I've noticed is mentioned in the book that the Red Talons &quot;give&quot; their cliaths to the Garou Nation in order to assist with the fight. That's basically what I was going to write down, you seem to know the Red Talons, would that be a rather unusual occurrence? I know that the World of Darkness theme is based on creativity, but since I wish to follow the main path set for my character by the lore, I'd like to know. And at the moment there are no Red Talons whatsoever in our game. (We're around 40 - 60 players playing this game on an online modifiable game, and so most characters must be real people and not NPCs - so no Red Talons)<br /> <br /> Thank you for the reply, you've helped me a lot!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23978-tatacavalier","name":"TataCavalier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T08:33:15-07:00","id":1194257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silentline</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193048-red-talons-in-packs-with-homid-garou?p=1193196#post1193196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey,<br /> <br /> -----------&gt;I've been recently thinking of creating a Red Talon character. So far all the knowledge I have of them is from their revised tribe book and from the core rule book of WtA 20th edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Well I'm glad to hear it player. Remember its not the things you know. It's the things you don't know that matter.&quot;<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> -Jerod the Glasswalker explained to the more open minded Red Talon as he tossed him some homid clothes to put on that they had to blend in with the crowd to slip past his gouls who were positioned throughout mall security to suprise the vampires who cleverly slept in a closed section of the mall. Once there they would tear those slumbering leeches to pieces.<br /> <br /> -Jerod Akbar turned to in horror to watch as the normal people stood, gawked, pointed, and a mother screamed covering her childs eyes in shock to see the Talon pack mate wearing no pans.-<br /> (Jerod)&quot; Mud-Blood!!! Where are your pans?! :O<br /> -Mud-Blood raised his his arm to reveal his left arm through the pans leg. Feeling a sense of achievement the Red Talon wagged his butt panting with tongue extended- C:<br /> (Jerod) OMFG..... -.-<br /> -Jerod- Another day at the office...<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------&gt;I know for a fact that they would and do run in packs with homids, but how often does it happen? Is it that common in modern times that it'd be given if my character were to be in a pack with homid Garou?<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes. But know most Red-Talon are closed minded and NOT subtle. During play try to always picture things from the standpoint of a wolf. The smells and what they would associate with it.. food or the scent of a rival mutt etc. Who's leader stands really, really high. And if your leader does not show alpha qualities your wolf nature will correct him in this fact.. brutally by<br /> a challenge because this is also linked to your rite to mate and this is a strong urge for them in survival. As a lupus you will do things softer homids may consider.. erm.. gross.. pissing in public on boundries is just one thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------&gt; Also, while I'm already posting a question, I'll use the moment to ask for sources to learn more about the Talons. Anything will do, since I want to be able to role play it the best I can.<br /> <br /> &quot;Try Caerns Places of Power - Red Talons Alaska (pg 77), Rage Across the world Vol. 2 (See Australian Red Talons section), of course the Red Talons Tribe book old to newer versions.<br /> If you want to get really outlandishly brutal with it also see Rage Across the Heavens (pg. 43-46 Rorg), and for an understanding of associated spirits Axis Mundi book of spirits and the Book of the Wyld in the event you play an accomplished Theurge.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Ultimately you design what you want to play and its story line which has formed its behavior up to the point of the chronicle. Remember.. you and weaver DO NOT MIX to many ends. The mating stock of the homids has killed off most of yours without being punished and in fact has been protected by other tribes instead. Inside a Red-Talon there is deeply seated anger towards that end. You are pro Wyld.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mhm. All of this is true, the first two messages I had already processed and was ready to role-play.<br /> About the third one though, while it is correct I feel that the pack of the bond is a bond that cannot be ignored. A Red Talon would love and cherish (in their own wolf way) his packmates, be them homid, lupus or metis. As The Luaghing Stranger said, there must be a good reason for them to have bonded so strongly.<br /> I'll have to agree that upon meeting a homid for the first time, a Red Talon would either be neutral or leaning towards disliking the Garou. But then, views of people change quickly, especially if you see the homid actively working to.. (just an example from the top of my head) save and protect the wolf population in his region. That would earn -major- points with a Red Talon.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thank you for taking your time to reply, you've helped very much! You all have! I'll keep planning this character and hopefully by this Friday I'll feel it's ready to be added to the game.<br /> <br /> Again, thank you very much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23978-tatacavalier","name":"TataCavalier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T10:52:07-07:00","id":1194572,"title":"","content":"Mhm. All of this is true, the first two messages I had already processed and was ready to role-play.<br /> About the third one though, while it is correct I feel that the pack of the bond is a bond that cannot be ignored. A Red Talon would love and cherish (in their own wolf way) his packmates, be them homid, lupus or metis. As The Luaghing Stranger said, there must be a good reason for them to have bonded so strongly.<br /> I'll have to agree that upon meeting a homid for the first time, a Red Talon would either be neutral or leaning towards disliking the Garou. But then, views of people change quickly, especially if you see the homid actively working to.. (just an example from the top of my head) save and protect the wolf population in his region. That would earn -major- points with a Red Talon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well said player. That bond can supersede all sorts of divisions which can go even deeper with play.<br /> <br /> Sounds like you are on your way to a great RP experience. Have Fun!<br /> <br /> and Your very welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline","name":"Silentline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T06:37:37-07:00","id":1195265,"title":"","content":"Do Homid Red Talons exist by the way? So a horny and slightly idiotic Red Talon is &quot;in heat&quot;, and in homid form. They get someone pregnant, or get pregnant. One of their resulting children is Garou. Would that produce Ronin essentially? Since the pup would never be accepted by the Tribe, I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T06:44:37-07:00","id":1195270,"title":"","content":"The cub would not be accepted by either the tribe or the tribal totem.<br /> It would very well be raised by another tribe who has lesser standards towards heritage, Children of Gaia, Bonegnawer, if female Black Fury, if suitable Stargazer. <br /> <br /> Only if the cub can't make the Rite of Passage into another tribe, it would be Ronin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T08:05:06-07:00","id":1196792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silentline</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193048-red-talons-in-packs-with-homid-garou?p=1194572#post1194572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mhm. All of this is true, the first two messages I had already processed and was ready to role-play.<br /> About the third one though, while it is correct I feel that the pack of the bond is a bond that cannot be ignored. A Red Talon would love and cherish (in their own wolf way) his packmates, be them homid, lupus or metis. As The Luaghing Stranger said, there must be a good reason for them to have bonded so strongly.<br /> I'll have to agree that upon meeting a homid for the first time, a Red Talon would either be neutral or leaning towards disliking the Garou. But then, views of people change quickly, especially if you see the homid actively working to.. (just an example from the top of my head) save and protect the wolf population in his region. That would earn -major- points with a Red Talon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well said player. That bond can supersede all sorts of divisions which can go even deeper with play.<br /> <br /> Sounds like you are on your way to a great RP experience. Have Fun!<br /> <br /> and Your very welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just about to finalize my character and see if it gets accepted by the storytellers. Thank you again and wish me luck!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193048-red-talons-in-packs-with-homid-garou?p=1194572#post1194572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Homid Red Talons exist by the way? So a horny and slightly idiotic Red Talon is &quot;in heat&quot;, and in homid form. They get someone pregnant, or get pregnant. One of their resulting children is Garou. Would that produce Ronin essentially? Since the pup would never be accepted by the Tribe, I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the knowledge I've gathered while doing research on my (future) Red Talon character, it is highly unlikely to happen that a Red Talon would simply go ahead and lie with a human. Most of them loathe (even if slightly) the humans and see them as the Wyrm's grasp on the world. If the humans didn't exist, the Wyrm would have no power whatsoever. Or so they believe.<br /> Of course, there are the less strict and extreme Red Talons, but still, a Red Talon is a Red Talon and they see themselves as wolves. And wolves don't mate with humans, do they?<br /> <br /> Anyway, as heinrich said, the cub would not be accepted by the tribe and totem, and simply transferred to a different tribe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23978-tatacavalier","name":"TataCavalier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T21:41:51-07:00","id":1197031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193048-red-talons-in-packs-with-homid-garou?p=1195265#post1195265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Homid Red Talons exist by the way? So a horny and slightly idiotic Red Talon is &quot;in heat&quot;, and in homid form. They get someone pregnant, or get pregnant. One of their resulting children is Garou. Would that produce Ronin essentially? Since the pup would never be accepted by the Tribe, I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Children are always the breed of the Mother, so the get pregnant isn't an option","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T05:59:37-07:00","id":1197152,"title":"","content":"EDIT: nvm it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23978-tatacavalier","name":"TataCavalier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T19:23:00-07:00","id":1197836,"title":"","content":"The example play pack in the Revised book had a Red Talon. Yeah you are free to have this, the thing likely is they represent a more liberal member of the Tribe. But often Red Talons are in small groups being a dying off tribe and have to be members of Septs with Homids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T09:16:02-07:00","id":1199083,"title":"","content":"I don't really know any specific sources about wolves' state of mind (apart of Jack London ;-), but <a href=\"http://Are We Smart Enough to Know How Smart Animals Are?\" target=\"_blank\">Frans de Waal</a>'s books would be helpful, for instance <i>Are We Smart Enough to Know How Smart Animals Are? . </i>They are written for a general public, have loads of funny anecdotes, and you could probably use a lot of what he says about monkeys or other animals for wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23992-tazmaniacs","name":"Tazmaniacs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T18:11:59-07:00","id":1199268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tazmaniacs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193048-red-talons-in-packs-with-homid-garou?p=1199083#post1199083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really know any specific sources about wolves' state of mind (apart of Jack London ;-), but <a href=\"http://Are We Smart Enough to Know How Smart Animals Are?\" target=\"_blank\">Frans de Waal</a>'s books would be helpful, for instance <i>Are We Smart Enough to Know How Smart Animals Are? . </i>They are written for a general public, have loads of funny anecdotes, and you could probably use a lot of what he says about monkeys or other animals for wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's written for the general public, but it also has a long, long list of carefully numbered citations (elaborated on pages 277-318), so it's a bit more robust than a set of anecdotes. I'd say chief among the takeaways is that, given how conservative evolution can be, it's not really reasonable to assume that other animals are completely and totally alien to the human mind. The human mind didn't come from out of a vacuum; it was shaped by the same forces that shaped all the other minds and living spaces. Extrapolating from that, you might want to constantly remind lupus players to think with their mouths and noses over their hands until they get the hang of it.<br /> <br /> (There's also a section specifically dealing with how humans perceive the actions of dogs and wolves relative to each other, and it's probably worth getting for W:tA just for that alone.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}